      "content": "It is very possible that your symptoms are brain fog or stress-induced, given your mention of poor sleep and high workload. Stress and sleep deprivation can temporarily disrupt your short-term memory and executive function, making basic words feel elusive. However, because these episodes feel \"scary\" and are \"sudden,\" it is important not to assume it's just stress without checking in with a healthcare professional. You should consider scheduling an appointment to rule out other underlying causes for sudden confusion before your stress takes a physical toll.",
